// K1.schema — the WRITER of the ENUM-AGAINST-INTEGER pair (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md
// §3, §4). AN ENUM VALUE RIDES UNDER ITS OWN KIND 30, carrying the reference
// to its variant name's id, whatever the declaration-side storage width. The
// kind closes an edit a shared integer kind left open: an enum field respelled
// as its raw `uint16`, or the reverse, is an ordinary kind mismatch in both
// directions, counted, with the field taking its default.
//
// K2 declares the same two field names with the two spellings SWAPPED, so one
// wire written here and read there names both directions at once.
package tblk1

enum Grade { Bronze, Silver, Gold }

table Root
{
    grade Grade
    raw   uint16
}
